From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:38:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/31] Add Doc's role router and the models, summarize and
 usage commands

- Roles map to a provider and model from the config: summary -> local
  Muse Glimmer, workhorse -> baseten Muse Spark Open, restore -> meta
  muse-spark-1.3 (fallback baseten), planner and judge -> meta
  muse-wonder-1.0, voice -> meta muse-voice-transcribe-1.0 (config
  only). --role-provider role=provider overrides one role for one run.
- The router redacts every prompt, needs a key, a configured price and
  budget room for hosted calls, records usage, and takes one explicit,
  logged fallback: a role's configured hosted fallback after its hosted
  provider fails after retries (never for a missing or rejected key or
  a used-up budget, and never from local). --local sends every role to
  the local provider and refuses any hosted call.
- doc models [--check] [--available]: each role's provider, model and
  key status (never the key); --check sends one tiny prompt per
  provider and shows latency, tokens and cost; --available lists model
  IDs from GET /models. A missing local server is said plainly.
- doc summarize <checkpoint-id>: reads checkpoint show and diff JSON
  from dmc, redacts, and asks the summary role for 2-3 sentences.
  --show-prompt prints exactly what would be sent and sends nothing.
- doc usage: tokens and estimated cost per provider against budgets.
- CI analyzes and tests doc/, driving the compiled bundle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 684f54c3a16ab602ba9cbd064addcff21449f3dd..4ab5536e18acb2e2b71eed4b81910a07f44df95b 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -27,3 +27,12 @@ jobs:
         run: dart run tool/smoke_bundle.dart build/ci-dmc/bundle/bin/dmc
       - if: runner.os == 'Windows'
         run: dart run tool/smoke_bundle.dart build/ci-dmc/bundle/bin/dmc.exe
+      # Doc (doc/) is a separate package; its tests drive the bundle built above.
+      - run: dart pub get --enforce-lockfile
+        working-directory: doc
+      - run: dart analyze --fatal-infos
+        working-directory: doc
+      - run: dart test --concurrency=1
+        working-directory: doc
+        env:
+          DMC_TEST_BIN: ${{ github.workspace }}/build/ci-dmc/bundle/bin/${{ runner.os == 'Windows' && 'dmc.exe' || 'dmc' }}
